From d400733ec45e46dd52c50583e246a238d600aeff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: decklink-linux-anon
 <358323356+decklink-linux-anon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:41:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] platform: DeckLink video output (Linux, 1080p25 UYVY)

Add filmcraft_platform::decklink: DeckLink device 0 driven at 1920x1080
25p, 8-bit Y'CbCr 4:2:2 (UYVY), BT.709 limited range.

- decklink/shim.cpp: a small C ABI over the DeckLink COM interfaces
  (open / display / close), compiled by build.rs with cc on Linux only.
  Every entry point catches C++ exceptions.
- decklink/sdk/: the unmodified DeckLink SDK 12.0 Linux include files
  (BSL-1.0, as redistributed by OBS Studio). DeckLinkAPIDispatch.cpp
  dlopen()s libDeckLinkAPI.so at run time, so builds need no Blackmagic
  software and machines without Desktop Video simply get an error.
- Output::open starts a thread that owns the device; Output::send hands
  it the newest R'G'B'A picture (an older one not yet shown is replaced).
  Output::stats reports shown / refused frames and conversion / push time.
- rgba_to_uyvy: integer table BT.709 conversion with aspect-preserving
  fit and black bars (about 6 ms a 1080p frame, was 42 ms in float).
- color_bars: a 75 % bars test picture.

unsafe stays in the FFI module (src/decklink/ffi.rs) with SAFETY
comments, per ADR 0001. NOTICE lists the vendored headers.
